<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian Social Union in Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CSU</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Christian Social Union in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> is a conservative political party founded in 1945 that operates only in Bavaria, where it has led the state government almost continuously since 1946. In federal politics it forms a joint parliamentary group with the Christian Democratic Union. Franz Josef Strauss was its dominant leader from 1961 to 1988.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-social-union-in-bavaria.jpg" alt="Christian Social Union in Bavaria" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThecentreCZ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Christian_Social_Union_in_Bavaria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
